+ nesnd_civic_routes.1.t: "The Work Becomes Routine"
+ nesnd_civic_routes.1.d: "The expenditure has entered the budget, and the workshops or schools have been tested by ordinary operation. Supporters can point to a tangible result; opponents still ask who bears the taxes and who receives the benefit. The undertaking now extends beyond its original advocates."
+ nesnd_civic_routes.1.a: "Let it endure."
+ nesnd_c2_project_target_tt: "Selected project state: [STATE.GetName]"
+ nesnd_c2_retarget: "Revise the Undertaking"
+ nesnd_c2_retarget_desc: "After the present funding term, choose a state within the current borders. Paid costs are not refunded; the new undertaking requires fresh observation."
+ nesnd_c2_local_industry: "Local Industrial Assistance"
+ nesnd_c2_local_school: "Local Education Arrangements"
+ nesnd_c2_local_transport: "Local Transport Cooperation"
+ nesnd_c2_local_pasture: "Pasture Passage Safeguards"
+ nesnd_c2_local_administration: "Local Fiscal Arrangements"
+ nesnd_c2_local_military: "Public Military Works"
+ nesnd_c2_italy_agenda: "The Italian Common Undertaking"
+ nesnd_c2_hus_agenda: "Land and People of the Republic"
+ nesnd_c2_usm_agenda: "Livelihoods Under the Constitution"
+ nesnd_c2_italy_agenda_reason: "The Lombard Republic has French support, but the Italian states retain their own revenues, armies and schools. Development can proceed under protection; both unification and lasting cooperation require concrete local commitments. French political credit cannot decide on another state’s behalf."
+ nesnd_c2_hus_agenda_reason: "Workshops, railways and trading houses continue to expand, while debt bonds, inherited privilege and pasture boundaries divide the republic’s freedoms. The government can choose contractors, schools and local distributions; the registration order remains a question for the existing laws and political struggle."
+ nesnd_c2_usm_agenda_reason: "The cabinet and Six Ministries propose policy; the Assembly of Rites considers constitutional law. Provincial administrators execute fiscal administration, while provincial delegates represent their provinces. Academy students learn useful arts and prepare for the Assembly’s examinations. Expanding schools and industry sharpens the dispute over who may enter public life and who must pay."
+ nesnd_c2_italian_propose_lom: "Negotiate Schools and Revenue with $LOM$"
+ nesnd_c2_italian_propose_sar: "Negotiate Schools and Revenue with $SAR$"
+ nesnd_c2_italian_propose_sic: "Negotiate Schools and Revenue with $SIC$"
+ nesnd_c2_italian_propose_pap: "Negotiate Schools and Revenue with $PAP$"
+ nesnd_c2_italian_propose_par: "Negotiate Schools and Revenue with $PAR$"
+ nesnd_c2_italian_propose_mod: "Negotiate Schools and Revenue with $MOD$"
+ nesnd_c2_italian_propose_tus: "Negotiate Schools and Revenue with $TUS$"
+ nesnd_c2_compact_expense: "Italian Accord Expenditure"
+ nesnd_c2_italian_propose_desc: "Each state funds twelve months of expenditure and maintains services in its own schools, administration or military establishments. The other state decides whether to accept. Three months of mutual fulfilment establish an accord. An unanswered proposal lapses after ninety days; talks may resume after twelve months."
+ nesnd_civic_routes.10.t: "Schools, Military Revenue and the States"
+ nesnd_civic_routes.10.d: "A neighbouring state proposes a shared public undertaking. Schools, local revenues and military expenses would become budgetary obligations for both governments. Each must fund services on its own territory. The proposal preserves both states and their borders; the decision is ours."
+ nesnd_civic_routes.10.a: "Accept the mutual obligations."
+ nesnd_civic_routes.10.b: "Ask for schools and local services first."
+ nesnd_civic_routes.10.c: "Decline the proposal."
+ nesnd_civic_routes.11.t: "Conditions from the Local Government"
+ nesnd_civic_routes.11.d: "The other government is willing to negotiate, but asks that schools and local services take precedence over military commitments. Both states would still fund and operate their own establishments. A letter of assent cannot replace those obligations."
+ nesnd_civic_routes.11.a: "Accept the proposed priorities."
+ nesnd_civic_routes.12.t: "The Talks End"
+ nesnd_civic_routes.12.d: "These talks have produced no workable agreement. Refusal, war or a change in political relations can remove the basis of a proposal. Each state remains responsible for its own schools, revenue and forces."
+ nesnd_civic_routes.12.a: "Proceed separately for now."
+ nesnd_civic_routes.13.t: "The States Fulfil Their Accord"
+ nesnd_civic_routes.13.d: "Both governments have maintained the promised services and borne the expenditure. Their cooperation now rests on something tangible in local life. Unification and lasting cooperation between states remain political choices."
+ nesnd_civic_routes.13.a: "Let the accord take root."
+ nesnd_c2_italy_direction_french_republic: "French-Supported Republican Integration"
+ nesnd_c2_italy_direction_french_republic_desc: "The Lombard Republic allows French support and Italian integration to proceed together. Republican institutions, public works and talks with each state will underpin this course. French credit does not replace their consent."
+ nesnd_c2_italy_direction_autonomous_concord: "Autonomous Cooperation"
+ nesnd_c2_italy_direction_autonomous_concord_desc: "Faced with concrete diplomatic obstacles, the government proposes cooperation through the states’ own budgets and commitments. Existing workshops and schools remain; relations with France will determine future policy."
+ nesnd_c2_italy_direction_southern_monarchy: "Southern Monarchical Integration"
